        "procedure": "H3L (0.03 g, 0.1 mmol) and Dy(dbm)3·2H2O (0.17 g, 0.2 mmol) were successively dissolved in a mixed solution of dichloromethane (3 mL) and MeOH (3 mL). The resulting solution was transferred into a 10 mL vial and kept in an oven at 80 °C for three days, then slowly cooled to room temperature. Yellow block-shaped crystals were separated by filtration, washed with dichloromethane and dried in air.",
